### 1. Obtain a synthetic local token (requires the `local` Spring profile)
# @name token
GET http://localhost:8080/local/demo-token?role=INCIDENT_WRITER

> {% client.global.set("writerToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2. Register a synthetic incident
# @name createIncident
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{writerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: portfolio-intake-001

{
  "title": "Payment worker cannot reach PostgreSQL",
  "stackTrace": "org.postgresql.util.PSQLException: Connection to payments-db refused at com.example.payments.Worker.run(Worker.java:42)",
  "source": "payment-worker",
  "severity": "HIGH"
}

> {% client.global.set("incidentId", response.body.id); %}

### 3. Obtain a reader token and retrieve the public incident contract
# @name readerToken
GET http://localhost:8080/local/demo-token?role=INCIDENT_READER

> {% client.global.set("readerToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/{{incidentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{readerToken}}

### 4. Request analysis (configure an Ollama or OpenAI profile for a successful model response)
# @name analystToken
GET http://localhost:8080/local/demo-token?role=ANALYST

> {% client.global.set("analystToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/incidents/{{incidentId}}/analyses
Authorization: Bearer {{analystToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: portfolio-analysis-001

### 5. Show safe failure handling when no model is configured
# With only the `local` profile, the previous request responds with 503 Problem Details,
# not an invented diagnosis. Start with `local,openai` or configure Ollama to demonstrate 201.
